INSERT INTO rsg.change_log (at, kind, title, details, ref, source) VALUES ('2026-11-15T14:31:08+00:00', 'deploy', 'Theme/rsg-core deploy to live', $q$- Hero polish: comparison subtitle moves under the title as the summary (review style); review summary → byline 24 px; proof item "No free samples" (fits on one line with How we review).
- Page section anchors (e.g. /about-2/#how-we-review) clear the sticky header.
- "How we review" links go to the new About-page section (/about-2/#how-we-review).
- rsg-core people: also skip the site's own host (staging).
- rsg-core people: sameAs accepts real host names only (a Website field holding junk passed the old check).
- Author schema: one rsg_schema_person() everywhere (jobTitle, image, sameAs, worksFor; same @id), author pages get ProfilePage + full Person (bio, knowsAbout), comparisons get an Article node (author, dates, publisher). rsg-core 0.5.1: writers' profile-link fields (Users → Contact Info) for sameAs. Byline: "N articles", role = short introduction field.
- Byline v3 fixes: review count includes GPS reviews (GPS writers showed 0) and hides at 0; phone proof row left-aligned (desktop rule outranked it), check icon top-aligned on wrapped items.
- Byline v3 (reviews + comparisons): shared rsg_trust_html() — "Tested by"/"Written by" + role + N reviews, dates in their own right-hand column (inline under the author on phones), tinted proof row (bought with our own money at <shop>, no free samples, How we review). One font size; replaces the run-on trust line.
- footer.php: remove the old GA affiliate_click handler for /go/ links (no page has /go/ links since the DFS price box switch on 10 Nov; checked 15 Nov on 11 page types).
- Comment count box keeps the h3's padding (.widget-title-bg h3 rule) after h3 -> p.h3.
- Article subtitle (dek) p.h4 instead of an h4 heading (same look).
- Article HTML for machines (item 9): extraction back to live's level after the article changes; boilerplate headings out.
- Schema dates: datePublished = post_date (what pages show; post_date_gmt is off by -7..+2 h on old posts), dateModified = last real text change but never earlier than published (rsg_schema_dates). Used by the review, old-review and article schema and og article:modified_time.
- Articles: byline + review-rule dates; structured data for old reviews, legacy /review/ and articles; user-rating scale fix.
- Articles' shoes box: disclosure line height inside article text; expanded list scrolls inside the sticky sidebar instead of running below the screen.
- Articles (posts + /content/): review layout with a sidebar and a 'Shoes in this article' box (Ruggero, 15 Nov).
- Newer-version notice, as chosen by Ruggero: card with the newer shoe's best price on old reviews; notice line on current reviews.
- Legacy trail notice readable on the hero photo (white box, ink text; the text was invisible on the image).
- Legacy trail reviews (/review/, include-single-review-trail.php): same 'There's a new version' notice under the hero title (rsg_newest_model_id). Speedgoat 2, Speedcross 5, Challenger ATR 6 etc. had none.
- Old reviews: 'There's a new version' notice links to the newest published review of the shoe line.
- Homepage: 'Brands buying guides' -> 'Reviews by brand' (guides cleanup 15 Nov). The 8 brand cards link to the brand's review listing (get_term_link = /reviews/<brand>/all/) instead of the retired brand guide; bottom button '+ All reviews' -> /reviews/.
- Guides cleanup follow-up: brand listing no longer fatals when its featured post is unpublished; /reviews/ intro and homepage 'View all guides' link to the hub /top/best-running-shoes-right-now/ (old targets: retired 2024 guide = 404, /guide/ archive).
- Step 5 item 2b: GPS phone bar keeps the Amazon button and Sections on one line.
- Step 5 item 2: GPS reviews' bottom table-of-contents pill (under Raptive's sticky ads on phones) replaced by the 'Sections' picker in the phone bar at the top, as on road/trail/training reviews. .rsg-dfs-toc CSS moved from rsg-dfs.css to rsg-skin.css (GPS reviews load no DFS CSS/JS; jump handler in the GPS template).
- Page-type check: author page kicker no longer overlapped by the name (h1.page-title > small + span margin).
- Comparison C7: photos for reviews published as blog posts. rsg_review_photo_id() (rsg-core): a review's photo N from its gallery, else from the photos in its text (2020-2022 reviews were blog posts without a gallery field: 59 of 346 comparison shoe links). Used by the share image and the page's photo band / 'which one to buy' pair.
- Comparison C6c: latest-comparison cards show the 1200x630 share image uncropped (aspect 40/21; 16/9 cut off the label and name tags).
- Comparison C6b: wp rsg-share takes several ids (## OPTIONS section in the command help); summary counts by status word.
- Comparison C6: automatic share + listing image (rsg-core 0.5.0, inc/share-image.php). 1200x630 JPEG from the first gallery photo of each review (our own test photos, same as the page's top band), VS badge, name tags, RUNNING SHOES GURU label; becomes the comparison's featured image (og:image, twitter:image, listing cards); previous featured image id kept in rsg_share_prev_thumb (wp rsg-share restore). Built on comparison save (save_post 20, after ACF) and by wp rsg-share build [<id>...|--all] [--force] [--dry-run]; rebuilt only when photos/names/version change. Skipped when a review has no gallery photo. Fonts: static TrueType instances of the theme fonts (SIL OFL), rsg-core/assets/fonts.
- Comparison C5: writer box + latest cards. Visible writer box at the end of the article (rsg_cmp_writer_box(): the review 'Reviewed by' component, 'Written by <first name>', 'All articles by', dates + bio in a <p>) replaces the hidden 'This expert review is written by' pop-up. 'Latest comparisons' (rsg_cmp_latest()): h2 + cards (image + title as one link, no h4 in cards, no yellow button; the old 'Read more' button linked to the image file) replaces RSG_print_related_block() and the empty Amazon widget include here.
- Comparison C3b: section text class rsg-cmp-sec (was rsg-cmp-text + Raptive marker rsg-text): a class containing "text" made readability keep only the prose (0/9 page items, 3.3k chars); without it 9/9, 4.7k (tested on the staging HTML). Raptive marker for comparisons comes with the ads work.
- Comparison C4: "Best price online" heading is an h2 (was h1, same text); the two price boxes stay side by side from 768 px in the 760 px column (compact boxes, 350 px each), stacked on phones; old spacer gone. The sidebar's "Compare all shops" lands here (#rsg-prices).
- Comparison C3: body sections. Sole unit / Upper unit / Which one to buy are h2 (were h1; same text) with the review reading rhythm (17/19 px, 18 px between paragraphs, bold highlighter) in div.rsg-cmp-text.rsg-text (Raptive marker); old spacers gone. Photo pairs on every comparison (rsg_cmp_pair(), same component as the top band, 4:3 in the 760 column): first photo of each review's sole_unit / upper text, and for "Which one to buy" the second gallery photo (was the reviews' stock featured images); no pair unless both photos exist. Inline photos in comparison text get the 760 px treatment (rsg_review_img_760 + comparison). rsg_cr_* helpers replaced by rsg_cmp_field_img() / rsg_cmp_pair().
- Comparison C2b: score bars + jump links, redesign block retired. Score breakdown = table.rsg-sc (shoe 1 value | label | shoe 2 value, 10-segment bars growing outwards from the label, higher score bold) + "Where each wins" lines; on every comparison whose two reviews have >= 3 sub-scores (was the orange/blue radar on the 3 redesign pages only). "In this comparison" jump links on all comparisons. includes/comparison-redesign-block.php removed: its photo-pair helpers moved unchanged into includes/comparison-snapshot.php (restyled in C3); its radar, chooser and duplicate computations are gone.
- Comparison C2a: photo band + snapshot card. Top: title and a band with the first gallery photo of each review (our own test photos, VS badge), full width above article + sidebar (the sidebar starts below it); no band when a shoe has no gallery (never the stock featured images). Snapshot card for every comparison (includes/comparison-snapshot.php, rsg_cmp_snapshot()): short verdict as its top row when filled, then a 2-shoe table.rsg-cmp (review compare table component): photo + name, expert score, user score, best price men/women, Buy if, review link, brand, type, weight (lighter), drop, cushioning, stability, flexibility, sizing, best for, retail price; pages without a short verdict keep the per-shoe Verdict row (desktop only, as before). Replaces the separate verdict box, the old snapshot and the "What matters most" chooser (redesign pages) and the "Similarity and differences" table (other pages; its heading stays, now h2).
- Comparison C1: page frame + top. Comparisons use the review layout: main#main.container > .row > article.col-lg-8.rsg-content (760 px) + aside.col-4.rsg-sidebar (sticky two-shoe price card rsg_prices_card_pair(), box code rail; "Compare all shops" jumps to #rsg-prices) from 1,140 px. Top: breadcrumb (all comparisons), title with "Comparison:" kicker, trust line (writer, published/updated, editorial policy, How we review). The subtitle and introduction fields stay first and in the same order, now as body text inside the article. Featured image no longer shown on the page (still the share/listing image). Extractors (simulated): trafilatura Clifton vs Bondi 3,258 -> 5,272 chars, 0/4 -> 4/4 items; Pegasus vs Clifton 3,320 -> 5,446, 0/3 -> 3/3; no new MISSING items.
- Reskin A4 (audit 15 Nov): mega-menu column titles are styled labels (<p class="h6">), not <h6> headings (12 of them, 2 empty, came before the page's h1 once the panels were printed in the page); each column's links are a <ul> labelled by its title (aria-labelledby); empty titles = empty div keeping the spacing; brand icons alt="" (link text names the brand). Same look. Object-cache key rsg_mega_menu_v2_ so the new markup shows at once.
- Merchant logos for AU: Running Warehouse AU, adidas (optical set, dfs/app/tools/logos/optical.py; existing logos byte-identical)
- Reskin A (audit 15 Nov): extractor fixes, same look. Trust box <aside> -> <section>; author box classes rsg-author* -> rsg-reviewer* and bio in a <p> (reviewer + "bought with our own money" back in extracted text); rating breakdown dl class rsg-ratings -> rsg-scores (extractors drop "rating" classes) and bar drawn by .rsg-rate::after from --v on the row (no empty aria-hidden <dd>); stack drawing <figure>/<figcaption> -> div.rsg-stack / div.rsg-stack-cap (extractors drop <figure>). trafilatura on Pegasus 42 (simulated): 46/69 -> 66/69 page items (live 65/69).
- Reskin 5.2: Raptive markers (additive). Body class per page type rsg-page-<type> (home, review, review-old, comparison, guide, toplist, article, listing, other; rsg_page_type() in rsg-core/inc/ads.php); review templates: rsg-content on the article, rsg-sidebar on the sidebar, rsg-text on the review text (so Raptive can switch content ads to the text only without a code change). Old structure kept until Raptive re-maps.$q$, 'live-20261115-143049', 'deploy.sh');
